on" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186137956 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186530010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186137956 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "545c0cdb-a270-5833-8eb2-8fcba0f8f682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138297 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138297 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $x^4-4x^2+4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15bbccd7-d0ce-50bb-80bb-777b5d0a7245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138297 #edb/ref 1074 "We can introduce a new variable $z=x^2$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+4 & = \\\\ {({x}^{2})}^{2}-4({x}^{2})+4 & = \\\\ {z}^{2}-4z+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a difference, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-4z+4 & = \\\\ (z-2)^{2} & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138304 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5018" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138304 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $t^4 - t^2 - 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12f9f52c-0baa-557b-83b7-d80c8a34c409" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138304 #edb/ref 1074 "We can introduce a new variable $z = t^2$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}-2 & = \\\\ {({t}^{2})}^{2}-{t}^{2}-2 & = \\\\ {z}^{2}-z-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-z-2 & = \\\\ (z+1)(z-2) & = \\\\ ({t}^{2}+1)({t}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138305 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138305 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $2p^4 + 5p^2 + 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138305 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f503abb5-10a5-56bf-b07b-7ebe1ed04049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138305 #edb/ref 1074 "We can introduce a new variable $t = p^2$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{p}^{4}+5{p}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ 2{({p}^{2})}^{2}+5{p}^{2}+3 & = \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+5t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+5t+3 & = \\\\ (t+1)(2t+3) & = \\\\ ({p}^{2}+1)(2{p}^{2}+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1039 "Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Perfect Squares" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138385 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a962db4f-c6bf-5631-95b2-c7f42b1236d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1039 "Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Quadratic Trinomials" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138411 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ee76fa0d-93f1-5b0b-b9e4-4c081741078e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138412 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138412 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138412 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17