z={u}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{4}+2{u}^{2}-3 & ={({u}^{2})}^{2}+2({u}^{2})-3 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}+2z-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}+2z-3 & =(z-1)(z+3) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-1)({u}^{2}+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
